{"credentialModelOpt.get() will throw NoSuchElementException when user has no recovery codes in either storage, causing a 500 error on the login page - need to handle the empty case explicitly": 0.8161776065826416, "generatedCodes are raw recovery codes being serialized and passed to updateCredential, which means user storage providers will store plaintext recovery codes instead of hashed values - need to hash before serialization using RecoveryAuthnCodesUtils::hashRawCode or serialize credentialModel's hashed data": 0.8871423602104187, "Using RecoveryAuthnCodesUtils.getCredential can return federated credentials, but cleanup uses removeStoredCredentialById which only removes from Keycloak's internal storage - federated recovery codes from external storage providers will never be deleted after all codes are used, should use disableCredentialType for federated credentials": 0.7252869606018066, "BackwardsCompatibilityUserStorage.disableCredentialType only handles OTP and needs to be updated to handle RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialModel.TYPE to clear federated recovery codes": 0.5920146703720093}